     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">in a study, we are interested in colour-feeling associations. For the study, participants were given 15 feelings (angry, furious, passionate etc.) and they had to select a colour from a set of 27 colour shades for each feeling.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">This is the result, the 27 colour shades were collapsed into 14 broader colour terms.</p><p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\"><br></p><table frame=\"VOID\" cellspacing=\"0\" cols=\"15\" rules=\"NONE\" border=\"0\" style=\"font-family:Arial;font-size:x-small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><colgroup><col width=\"89\"><col width=\"49\"><col width=\"42\"><col width=\"56\"><col width=\"123\"><col width=\"53\"><col width=\"43\"><col width=\"113\"><col width=\"62\"><col width=\"41\"><col width=\"56\"><col width=\"35\"><col width=\"32\"><col width=\"49\"><col width=\"56\"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td width=\"89\" height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\"><br></td><td width=\"49\" align=\"LEFT\">black</td><td width=\"42\" align=\"LEFT\">blue</td><td width=\"56\" align=\"LEFT\">brown</td><td width=\"123\" align=\"LEFT\">colour.not.listed</td><td width=\"53\" align=\"LEFT\">green</td><td width=\"43\" align=\"LEFT\">grey</td><td width=\"113\" align=\"LEFT\">no.association</td><td width=\"62\" align=\"LEFT\">orange</td><td width=\"41\" align=\"LEFT\">pink</td><td width=\"56\" align=\"LEFT\">purple</td><td width=\"35\" align=\"LEFT\">red</td><td width=\"32\" align=\"LEFT\">tile</td><td width=\"49\" align=\"LEFT\">white</td><td width=\"56\" align=\"LEFT\">yellow</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">angry</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">71</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">bored</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">34</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">19</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">15</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">9</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">calm</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">40</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">9</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">18</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">6</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">cheerful</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">8</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">6</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">10</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">50</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">confident</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">5</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">16</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">6</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">12</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">8</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">18</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">9</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">depressed</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">28</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">27</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">11</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">12</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">excited</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">5</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">13</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">11</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">6</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">21</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">fearful</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">19</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">5</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">19</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">16</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">furious</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">67</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">happy</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">6</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">10</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">5</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">5</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">46</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">jealous</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">47</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">9</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">16</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">joyful</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">10</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">8</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">12</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">43</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">passionate</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">11</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">55</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">sad</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">3</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">54</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">9</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">6</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td></tr><tr><td height=\"18\" align=\"LEFT\">shy</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">11</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">11</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">1</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">10</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">14</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">0</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">7</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">9</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">9</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">4</td><td align=\"RIGHT\">2</td></tr></tbody></table>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">For the results, we are interested in which associations are particularly strong. </p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">My initial idea was to perform a chisquare test on the contingency table, and to plot the residuals to show which associations are significant and which ones are repelled.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">However, there are many zeros in the contingency table which means that a chisquare test should not be performed. </p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">If I perform a fisher test, I get the following error message:</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">“Error in fisher.test(english) : FEXACT error 5.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">The hash table key cannot be computed because the largest key</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">is larger than the largest representable int.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">The algorithm cannot proceed.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Reduce the workspace size or use another algorithm.”</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Irrespective of the fisher test, in order to get at the residuals to compute strength of association, I have to perform the chisquare test. But again, I am not sure whether I can do this, given all the zeros in my contingency table.</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Shall I refrain from analysing the residuals and look at percentages instead?</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Thanks for your help!</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica;min-height:14px\"><br></p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Best,</p>\r\n<p style=\"font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Helvetica\">Nina</p><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "LdEz8DOgDwAJ",
   "from": "Stefan Th. Gries",
   "author": "3edc58ee737edd94",
   "date": "2019-07-22T11:06:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: [StatForLing with R] large contingency tables with many zeros",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">My first thought would be to go with association rules (packages arules and arulesViz, I think), which can return values that tell you very similar things to residuals etc. Of course, arules are also somewhat sensitive to the extremely small n you have (for that many cells), like any approach would be, but measures such as support, confidence, and lift might be useful to explore the kinds of data you have.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div>HTH,</div><div>STG</div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "loKDRT1xEAAJ",
   "from": "Nina Julich",
   "author": "5bac756205e8499c",
   "date": "2019-07-22T11:13:13Z",
   "subject": "Re: [StatForLing with R] large contingency tables with many zeros",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Ok. Thank you! I will have a look at association rules.<div>Just to make sure, you would definitely advise against using residuals retrieved from a chisquare test?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Nina</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Am Montag, 22. Juli 2019 13:06:48 UTC+2 schrieb Stefan Th. Gries:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">My first thought would be to go with association rules (packages arules and arulesViz, I think), which can return values that tell you very similar things to residuals etc. Of course, arules are also somewhat sensitive to the extremely small n you have (for that many cells), like any approach would be, but measures such as support, confidence, and lift might be useful to explore the kinds of data you have.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div>HTH,</div><div>STG</div></div>\n</blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "bxZvQ0ujDwAJ",
   "from": "Stefan Th. Gries",
   "author": "3edc58ee737edd94",
   "date": "2019-07-22T12:03:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: [StatForLing with R] large contingency tables with many zeros",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "&gt; Just to make sure, you would definitely advise against using residuals retrieved from a chisquare test?\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "I wouldn&#39;t go that far (and some of the association rules statistics\r<br>are in fact similar to the residuals) but of course they can become\r<br>quote inflated given the low expected frequencies and so a combination\r<br>of association rules statistics might help with filtering out\r<br>interesting things. You&#39;ll have to be creative ...\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
