  {
   "id": "aCS9-NeFEAAJ",
   "from": "ekbrown77",
   "author": "8dafe35eb614235f",
   "date": "2019-07-22T17:30:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: large contingency tables with many zeros",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Another nice visualization for categorical data is the association plot (as Stefan presents in his book). Base R&#39;s <a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/graphics/versions/3.5.3/topics/assocplot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/graphics/versions/3.5.3/topics/assocplot&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243554470000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3A_PVWVFErCuxoplOg_Eis\">assocplot()</a> function is alright, but I like <a href=\"https://rdrr.io/cran/vcd/man/assoc.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/cran/vcd/man/assoc.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243554470000&amp;usg=AOvVaw15QtHgjZDbQpMbYapYzFTl\">vcd::assoc()</a>, as it color-codes Pearson residuals in the plot. There&#39;s a good example <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=NFI_DwAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PA185&amp;lpg=PA185&amp;dq=vcd+assocplot&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=evShCEUw4e&amp;sig=ACfU3U3fqikYCa55QMm89WGcqIqdmz2kxQ&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjrl9rGhMnjAhWTvJ4KHSgNDM8Q6AEwEnoECAkQAQ#v=onepage&amp;q=vcd%20assocplot&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://books.google.com/books?id%3DNFI_DwAAQBAJ%26pg%3DPA185%26lpg%3DPA185%26dq%3Dvcd%2Bassocplot%26source%3Dbl%26ots%3DevShCEUw4e%26sig%3DACfU3U3fqikYCa55QMm89WGcqIqdmz2kxQ%26hl%3Den%26sa%3DX%26ved%3D2ahUKEwjrl9rGhMnjAhWTvJ4KHSgNDM8Q6AEwEnoECAkQAQ%23v%3Donepage%26q%3Dvcd%2520assocplot%26f%3Dfalse&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243554470000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0aJ8QUl-ab34D45A_rS0-H\">here</a>, as well as in <a href=\"https://benjamins.com/sites/z.195/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://benjamins.com/sites/z.195/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243554470000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2F3qv8sI0pEfnbYkGn2bqf\">Levshina (2015)</a>. </div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
